+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-11-add-cancellation/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+## Why
+
+Customers change their plans and ask the booking desk to cancel rentals. The cancellation policy is already recorded in the equipment-rental spec, but the service offers no way to cancel, so the desk cannot release equipment or tell the customer what is refunded.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `cancel(bookingId, at)` to the rental service: it cancels the booking at time `at` and returns `{ bookingId, refund }`.
+- The refund follows the existing cancellation policy: the full total at least 24 hours before the start of the booking, otherwise 0.
+- A cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment: `book` and `availability` treat its period as free.
+- A booking can be cancelled only once; unknown ids, invalid `at` and repeated cancellations throw.
+
+## Scope
+
+In scope: rentals (boards and sails, by the day or by the hour) cancelled through the service.
+Out of scope: partial refunds, cancellation fees, rescheduling, customers and lessons, enforcing the April to October season.
+
+No runtime dependency is introduced.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `equipment-rental`: adds a cancellation requirement, and updates the cancellation policy, booking and availability behavior for cancelled bookings.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`: `RentalService` gains `cancel`; bookings get a cancelled state.
+- `test/rental.test.ts`: new tests.
